  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grenada is developing a new Decent Work Country Programme through a national tripartite process. At the same time, the country is reviewing key labour laws to strengthen coherence and alignment with international labour standards, including on occupational safety and health and the effectiveness of dispute prevention and resolution. During the biennium, the ILO works with workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations to strengthen their capacity to develop integrated and evidence-informed trade union proposals and to have these proposals considered in policymaking. It also aims to strengthen workers&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; organizations&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; capacity to participate in Decent Work Country Programme implementation, monitoring and evaluation and to engage effectively in labour law reform discussions. Workers, including women and other workers in vulnerable situations, benefit through stronger representation and more inclusive social dialogue, while national institutions benefit from clearer, more coherent and more participatory policy development.</narrative>
  </description>
